{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SESSION HANDOVER — NOT closed. All four ACs verified; the close was REFUSED by the attestation-laundering gate on a fixable description-shape problem. No --force was used.\n\nMerge SHA: 3b92fad7df3c5d72dec5af269090e88e82640018 (\"Refresh scoped keys before diff (bug f449)\"), an ancestor of origin/main ae4f6c1a07a9. Gerrit change 2266: MERGED, LLM-Review approved, Verified approved.\n\nWHAT BLOCKS THE CLOSE (do this first):\n\"rebar transition f449-be6a-be56-4fef in_progress closed --class preexisting --ref ae4f6c1a07a9666adfbd7882e06d11dade61966a\" exits 1 with:\n  \"has [non-codebase] Acceptance Criteria items whose evidence is repository-resident (attestation laundering) ... cites: test_live_rich_text_renders_and_echo_is_safe, test_live_rich_text_both_sides_conflict_keeps_local\"\nCause: I named the two live test symbols inside AC3's provenance justification, which makes the criterion look repo-verifiable. REMEDY (the error's own instruction): SPLIT AC3 — move the repo-verifiable half (the two test names / their file) to a NEW UNTAGGED criterion, and keep only the external outcome (\"a dispatched Live External Integration run shows the DC lane and the Cloud mutation lane GREEN\") under [non-codebase] with a provenance: line that names NO repo paths or symbols. Validate the rewrite with rebar.llm.plan_review.det_measurement_provenance.provenance_gaps/provenance_issues (both must be []) BEFORE writing. That description edit is a MATERIAL change, so re-run \"rebar review-plan f449-be6a-be56-4fef --ref <pinned sha>\" (15-20 min) before retrying the close.\n\nPLAN-REVIEW STATE (already earned, will be staled by the split): review-plan at --ref ae4f6c1a07a9666adfbd7882e06d11dade61966a returned PASS, 0 blocking, 9 advisory, and the attestation is certified (currency_basis=file_impact). An earlier review at --ref 3b92fad7 also PASSed but went stale-code immediately: run_differs.py and test_dc_rich_text_live.py both changed on main AFTER the fix (6fe5c0d54574 and a3fee570874a) — so pin the review and the close to ae4f6c1a (or newer), NOT to 3b92fad7. The f449 fix itself is intact at ae4f6c1a (run_differs.py:237 still calls refresh_scoped_snapshot(ctx)).\n\nfile_impact: the 5 recorded paths are byte-identical to the 5 files 3b92fad7 touched (verified by diff of the two sorted lists). No set-file-impact call was needed or made.\n\nCLOSE CLASS chosen: preexisting — docs/ticket-model.md defines it as \"a latent defect that predated the work\". The defect is the level-triggered bound-field inbound differ (_diff_jira_vs_local) arbitrating against the fetcher's eventually-consistent JQL-search snapshot with no baseline; that seam long predates this ticket and was merely EXPOSED by the live DC harness. It is not a regression (no prior fix reintroduced), not plan_defect (the plan was right once corrected), not env_integration (the fix is a product change in rebar's reconciler, not an environment change), and not flaky (the failure was deterministic on a starved instance).\n\nPER-AC EVIDENCE:\nAC1 (root cause confirmed, with history/ADR support) — resolution #1 (PRODUCT), relocated to the correct layer: INBOUND, not outbound. Verified in merged code: outbound_field_diff.py defines _INBOUND_MIRRORED_FIELDS = {title, description, priority, status, assignee} (L47) and _suppressed_by_inbound (L330) is consulted for every one of them, so after rebar's own push local==baseline suppresses outbound and the same-pass bidirectional suppression cannot fire; inbound_differ._diff_jira_vs_local takes only (jira_fields, local_ticket) with no baseline/prev parameter, confirming it is level-triggered. CAVEAT / DEFECT FOUND: the citation \"ADR 0037 s3\" for the unbounded DC reindex (in the ticket body AND twice in snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py's module docstring) is WRONG — docs/adr/0037 is \"oss-contribution-intake-posture\". The real support is docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md L282 (\"Search-index lag (DC's Lucene index is eventually consistent)\"). The plan reviewer independently flagged the same stale citation as advisory. Worth a follow-up ticket to fix the docstring.\nAC2 (fix removes the unbounded-search-visibility dependency; held-out test with teeth) — snapshot_lagfree_refresh.overlay_lagfree_scalars direct-GETs via outbound_differ._safe_get_issue (immediately consistent) and MERGES the 5 mirrored scalars into curr_snapshot in place; refresh_scoped_snapshot is called at run_differs.py:237, ahead of both differs and _advance_baselines. test_dc_rich_text_live.py no longer contains _wait_until_search_reflects or any reindex call (grep: zero hits). LIVENESS ANCHOR: the oracle pairs a NEGATIVE CONTROL with the positive — test_stale_snapshot_would_clobber_without_the_overlay proves a stale snapshot genuinely emits exactly 1 inbound mutation carrying \"OLD body\", so test_overlay_prevents_the_inbound_clobber's \"== []\" is not reachable by the behaviour never running. MUTATION CHECK (M1): seeding \"return 0\" at the top of overlay_lagfree_scalars (seed verified present in the file before running) made 5 tests FAIL, including test_overlay_prevents_the_inbound_clobber; production file restored and \"git diff --quiet\" confirmed clean. SURVIVING MUTANT (M2, reported not fixed): replacing the run_differs.py:237 call with a no-op reference SURVIVES the entire tests/unit/rebar_reconciler suite (3637 passed, rc 0) — the overlay's BEHAVIOUR has teeth but its WIRING into run_differs has no offline coverage; only the live DC lane catches it. A regression test asserting refresh_scoped_snapshot runs during the diff phase would close that gap (candidate follow-up).\nAC3 [non-codebase] (dispatched Live External Integration run) — https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33137402410, workflow_dispatch on main at 6fe5c0d54574 (contains 3b92fad7), conclusion success. Job 98740362395 \"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)\" concluded success: 74 passed, 1 skipped, 1 xfailed. LIVENESS ANCHOR: both rich-text tests are recorded PASSED in the job log, not skipped, and the only SKIPPED line in that job is the unrelated agentic probe (no LLM credential). The \"jira Cloud coordinator mutation probe (bounded, self-cleaning, real Cloud)\" job also concluded success. Contrast run 33069684006, dispatched at 3b92fad7 itself, where the DC job FAILED — so a green DC lane is not the trivially-reachable state.\nAC4 (make lint && make typecheck && make test green) — make lint rc=0 and make typecheck rc=0 at HEAD ae4f6c1a in a clean worktree (the anthropic 1.2.0 typecheck break is an env artifact; pinned with 'anthropic<1'). make test could NOT be completed end-to-end in this session: three attempts were each terminated by the agent harness at 60-68%. Sharded instead: tests/e2e+interfaces+lib+scripts+golden = 3490 passed and tests/unit/rebar_reconciler+commands+plan_review = 3937 passed (rc 0), i.e. 7427 tests with ZERO genuine failures. IMPORTANT ENVIRONMENT ARTIFACT: the first shard reported 21 failures, ALL in tests/interfaces CLI help contracts asserting \"usage: rebar ...\"; the cause is FORCE_COLOR=3 in the shell environment injecting ANSI codes ahead of \"usage:\". Re-running those 5 files with FORCE_COLOR unset: 121 passed, rc 0. Not repository evidence — future sessions must run the suite with FORCE_COLOR unset. The remaining tests/unit top-level modules were NOT run locally; CI's Verified +1 on change 2266 covers the full suite for the merged commit.\n\nNEXT SESSION, IN ORDER: (1) split AC3 as described and re-validate provenance offline; (2) re-run review-plan --ref ae4f6c1a07a9666adfbd7882e06d11dade61966a; (3) retry the close with --class preexisting and the SAME pinned ref; (4) verify with \"rebar verify-signature f449-be6a-be56-4fef --kind completion-verifier\" — it must report certified, and exit 0 alone is not proof. Optionally file follow-ups for the ADR-0037 mis-citation and the M2 wiring-coverage gap."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787976844958283001,"uuid":"249dc63e-c924-4460-b4dd-a20abecd4ead"}